src/config/gate-coverage.yml:525

# road-to-source-silence Phase 2.1. This gate is DIFF-SCOPED, so redacting a
# confidentiality reference in this archived roadmap pulled the whole file into
# scope and surfaced a PRE-EXISTING line the gate had never looked at.
#
# The flagged string is an `ENC1:` ciphertext — the encrypted-link mechanism
# `source-confidentiality` MANDATES for a retained source link, produced by
# `src/scripts/_lib/link_crypto.ts`. It is high-entropy by construction, which
# is the whole point, and it is not a credential: it decrypts to a source URL,
# and the key is not in the tree.
#
# Fixed here rather than with an inline `<!-- secret-allow -->` marker on the
# line itself, deliberately: that line is in the ARCHIVE, and ADR-250
# authorises exactly one kind of edit to an archived roadmap — a confidentiality
# redaction that changes no decision, measurement or count. A scanner marker is
# not that, so it does not belong there.
#
# Line-pinned per this file's contract: if the line drifts, the gate REDS and
# someone re-audits.
